      "text": "The Stokes phenomenon for the Ramanujan’s q -diﬀerence equation and its higher order extension — We show connection formulae of local solutions of the Ramanu- jan equation between the origin and the\n\n**The Stokes phenomenon for the Ramanujan’s q -diﬀerence equation and its higher order extension**\n\n*Takeshi MORITA∗*\n\n22 pp, 10 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We show connection formulae of local solutions of the Ramanu- jan equation between the origin and the inﬁnity. These solutions are given by the Ramanujan function, the q-Airy function and the diver- gent basic hypergeometric series 2ϕ0(0, 0; −; q, x). We use two diﬀerent q-Borel-Laplace resummation methods to obtain our connection for- mulae. We also introduce the q-Borel-Laplace transformation of level r−1, which are higher order extension of these transformations. These methods are useful to obtain an asymptotic formula of a divergent se- ries rϕ0(0, 0, . . . , 0; −; q, x).\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 Basic notations; 3 Two q-exponential functions; 4 Covering transformations; 5 The Ramanujan function and the q-Airy functi; 6 The q-Borel-Laplace transformations; 7 The connection formula of the series 20(0,0;; 8 The q-Airy equation around the infinity and ; 9 The q-Borel-Laplace transformations of level",
